WEBVTT

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:07.190
<i>Tonegawa Yukio.</i>

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:10.650
<i>The razor-witted number 
two of the Teiai Group.</i>

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.260
<i>After pushing Kaiji to the brink,</i>

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>his exceptional skills are turned 
against him, leading to defeat.</i>

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.140
<i>As President Hyoudou Kazutaka's 
right-hand man,</i>

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.010
<i>he proudly steps forward 
to repent for his failure.</i>

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.790
<i>This is from before he met Kaiji...</i>

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.550
<i>In the shadow of the glory and the legends,</i>

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:36.750
<i>he serves as middle manager, suffering 
and fighting in ways no one knows...</i>

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
of a remarkable man.</i>

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:54.110
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:54.110
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:22.280
<i>Agenda 02
<b></b></i>Conjecture

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.500
<i>The Teiai Group's king,</i>

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:26.130
<i>President Hyoudou, has directly commanded</i>

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>one of his executives to concoct 
a diabolical game of death...</i>

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.350
<i>That man is Tonegawa Yukio!</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.800
<i>He assembles a project team</i>

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.180
<i>and immediately begins 
the first planning meeting.</i>

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.140
<i>But the first day is full of slip-ups!</i>

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:48.240
<i>It's already hard enough to tell these 
suited, sunglassed workers apart...</i>

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.130
<i>But then we have Yamazaki, 
Kawasaki, Ogino, Hagio:</i>

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.940
<i>a full fusillade of confusing names!</i>

00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.670
<i>Agitation! Irritation! Indignation!</i>

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:04.200
<i>Tonegawa makes the mistake of losing 
his cool! In front of his men!</i>

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.700
How the hell do I tell you apart?!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.210
<i>The men in black are, naturally, bewildered.</i>

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.710
<i>You're off to a terrible start, Tonegawa!</i>

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:17.710
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.720
<i>And the next day...</i>

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.110
<i>He returns to Meeting Room 3!</i>

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:55.330
Well, starting today, we'll be 
discussing the core of this project,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:59.220
the specifics of what kind 
of game we'll be running.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:04.010
To do that, the first and most 
important thing we need is ideas.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.010
More than anything else, we need ideas!

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.790
I want any clever or bright 
suggestions that might make for

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.150
a diabolical diversion with which 
to amuse the president.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.890
<i>Tonegawa decides to act like 
nothing happened yesterday</i>

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.730
<i>and make a passionate appeal.</i>

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.990
<i>However!</i>

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.990
<b>However!</b>

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.530
<i>Silence.</i>

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.240
<i>Absolute silence, like the bottom of the sea,</i>

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.760
<i>beyond the reach of both light and sound!</i>

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.520
What's wrong? Why so quiet?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.650
A bunch of people dressed in 
black, not saying a word...

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.400
What is this, a wake?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:19.170
I'll have you know, the president 
is still alive and well!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:30.600
<i>I took the risk of using the president 
as a punchline, and still no response!</i>

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.000
<i>"If I say something stupid, 
it'll piss him off."</i>

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.850
<i>Maybe I've given them that impression...</i>

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.510
<i>Beset by the pressure Tonegawa radiates</i>

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:43.360
<i>and the overwhelming fear of 
saying anything foolish...</i>

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:50.120
<i>As the intensity only grows more extreme, 
the men in black all think...</i>

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.670
<i>"I want just to clam up."</i>

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.380
Wait! Listen to me!

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:05.610
<i>Unable to bear the tension, 
Tonegawa is rejected by all the men!</i>

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:07.550
<i>Stonewalled! Ignored!</i>

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.890
<i>Tonegawa is totally isolated!</i>

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.520
<i>At this rate, we're going to end the meeting 
without accomplishing a damn thing!</i>

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.020
<i>In that case...</i>

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.570
Now, there's one thing 
I forgot to mention...

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:32.860
As you all know, this project is a 
proposal from President Hyoudou himself.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.610
In other words, the success 
of this project will

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.920
directly affect his appraisal of the team!

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:45.630
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:50.770
And that doesn't apply exclusively to me.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.460
After all, I intend to push!

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:52.950
<b>Push!</b>

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.670
If anyone contributes something 
of note to this project,

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:00.890
I will be reporting it to the president!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.880
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:03.490 --> 00:07:08.280
<i>Tonegawa provides encouragement! 
And then... even more!</i>

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:08.280
<b>Encouragement!</b>

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:08.280
<b>Encouragement!</b>

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:14.180
And to prove that, I've memorized each 
and every one of your names and faces!

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.670
Yamazaki!

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.580
Sir!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.700
Kawasaki!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:18.330
Sir!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.340
Saemon-saburou!

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:21.080
Sir!

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.140
Gonda!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:22.850
Sir!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:28.840
Gonda

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:23.760
Nakata!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:28.840
Nakata

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:24.260
Sir!

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.190
Doushita!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:25.930
Sir!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:28.840
Doushita

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:26.880
Nagata!

00:07:26.650 --> 00:07:28.840
Nagata

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.480
Sir!

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.230
Kikuchi!

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:28.840
Kikuchi

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:28.840
Sir!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.720
And you're... Hagio!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.290
You're Ogino!

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.220
Or rather...

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.900
You're Ogino!

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:41.930
Right!

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:43.860
And you're Hagio!

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:44.940
Right!

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:47.360
That was perfect, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:53.610
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:00.020
<i>He notices the faintest rumbling.</i>

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.680
<i>A stirring in their hearts!</i>

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:05.420
Do you people still not 
realize what I'm saying?!

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.050
This is our chance!

00:08:09.560 --> 00:08:13.930
An unprecedented chance for 
us to move up the ladder!

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:24.940
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:24.640
<i>Tonegawa's passion overwhelmed 
the men in black at first...</i>

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:27.750
<i>But now they're pushing forward!</i>

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:43.830
Excuse me... may I?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.310
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.490
Finally, we have a hero 
willing to blaze a trail.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.010
Let's hear it, Saemon-saburou.

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:59.010
What about a game based 
on rock-paper-scissors?

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.540
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.020
Huh? Rock-paper-scissors?

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:07.500
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:11.030
Well, I haven't thought about 
the specifics of the game yet,

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:15.190
but I was thinking maybe some kind 
of modified version of it might be fun.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:21.790
<i>Tonegawa thinks: "So give some ideas 
as to what these modified rules should be!"</i>

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:30.540
<i>But if he says that, it would shatter the 
atmosphere he's managed to cultivate!</i>

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:36.210
<i>They would all clam up again. 
It'd all be for nothing.</i>

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.560
Interesting.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.100
I see!

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:45.120
Everyone knows the rules 
of rock-paper-scissors,

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.540
so it'd be hard for any player to get the sense
that they're being cheated in that regard.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.170
Hey, Ebitani.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.210
Yes, sir!

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:56.180
Looks like we've already got one good idea.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.820
Thank you, sir!

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.700
What else have you got?

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.160
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.960
Here! Over here! I've got one!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.880
What about a game of mahjong where 
you gamble your own blood?

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:15.880
Now that's what I call diabolical!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:18.260
How about a contest where 
they face a wild animal?

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.760
Excellent!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.840
Electrified jump rope!

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:21.670
Outstanding!

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.720
A puzzle using the human body!

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:23.760
Sublime!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:24.890
<i>He praises!</i>

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.060
<b>Praise!</b>

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.890
<i>Regardless of anything else, he praises!</i>

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.890
<b>Praise! Praise! Praise!</b>

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:27.890
<b>Praise!</b>

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.300
<i>Even if the ideas are totally useless!</i>

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.660
I've got another one!

00:10:32.570 --> 00:10:33.660
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:34.580
Hypothetically...

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.360
I have another idea!

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.400
I remember an old game!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.400
Listen to mine!

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:37.550
<i>A landslide!</i>

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:41.660
<i>A landslide of suggestions, 
all hoping to win the boss's approval!</i>

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:47.200
They're all chirping now, like hatchlings!

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.920
Like little bulbul chicks, 
begging their mother for food!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.040
But that's good.

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:54.040
<b>Good.</b>

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:58.090
To get a lot of ideas out of a meeting,

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:01.220
first you need to cultivate an atmosphere 
where it's easy to make suggestions.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:02.980
And then you polish it off...

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:05.330
<b>Humor!</b>

00:11:03.690 --> 00:11:05.330
with a little humor!

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:08.810
Tonegawa-sensei! Tonegawa-sensei! 
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:11.060
Who am I, Prince Shotoku?!

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:12.360
Huh?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.540
<b>Huh...?</b>

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.320
You're all talking at once...

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:20.730
Am I supposed to be 
Prince Shotoku or something?!

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:22.320
<b>Prince Shotoku</b>

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.330
<b>Roar!</b>

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.340
<i>Good, good...</i>

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.590
I've taken control!

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:47.220
A little humorous lubricant has gotten 
these rusty wheels turning again!

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:52.450
Now we just need to roll 
out as a united front!

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.690
Who's that? Out of the way!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.370
Do you want to get run over?!

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:04.360
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:09.130
<i>At that moment, Tonegawa is 
struck by an ominous portent!</i>

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:13.120
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:13.120
<b>Portent!!</b>

00:12:09.130 --> 00:12:12.210
<i>He feels a chill like death 
itself is approaching!</i>

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:13.120
<b>Chills!</b>

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.120
<i>And fear!</i>

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:13.120
<b>Fear!!</b>

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:18.270
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.090
P-President Hyoudou!

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.790
<i>The emperor has descended.</i>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:58.340
<i>With the appearance of President Hyoudou, 
the mood in Meeting Room 3 has changed.</i>

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.630
<i>The air becomes electric... 
The mood... intense.</i>

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:05.760
I just wanted to check on things.

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.890
Am I getting in the way?

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:11.010
N-No, sir! Of course not!

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:13.900
Well, how are things going, then?

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:16.870
W-Well, we've currently 
come up with the themes...

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:19.920
An RPS-based game   Killer cops and robbers
Blood-draining Mahjong       Games of endurance
Clapping Game (Killer ver.)            Infinite Old Maid
Wild Animal battles   Full-Scale Board Game
Electrified jump rope                 Human Shogi
Dark poker               Monopoly man
UNO       Sky-high Rope Climb
Tag        Human Body Puzzle
Real Werewolf

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.050
The broad ideas for what 
to base the games around!

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.610
Ideas, eh?

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:23.770
And which are you going with?

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:29.570
Which of these ideas are you 
going to choose in the end?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.270
Well?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.830
We were just about to decide that...

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:35.530
Just now?

00:13:38.290 --> 00:13:42.670
<i>The president is killing all 
the momentum I had built up...</i>

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.420
<i>I need to find a way to get him out of here.</i>

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.250
President, why don't you—

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:49.930
Have a seat?

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.930
Down we go.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.450
Ebitani...

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.440
<b>Ebitani: Totally Clueless!</b>

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.440
<i>Ebitani: Totally Clueless!</i>

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:06.950
Go on.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:08.850
Right...

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.390
<i>Not a single misstep can be made.</i>

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:16.080
<i>Extreme tension and fear 
seize the men in black!</i>

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.280
<i>Even Tonegawa will be done for, 
should he fail here!</i>

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:32.210
Now then, I'd like to hear what 
each of you think are the winners

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:35.020
among the options we have so far.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:36.520
Yamazaki!

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.930
Sir?!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:39.940
Which is it?!

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:46.410
<i>Tonegawa-sensei encouraged us 
to suggest a bunch of ideas...</i>

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:51.950
Blood-draining Mahjong
Clapping Game (Killer ver.)
Wild Animal battles
Electrified jump rope
Dark poker
UNO
Tag

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:47.690
<i>But now that I look at them,</i>

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.950
<i>they're all a bunch of 
random, half-baked suggestions!</i>

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:51.950
<i>Which one is actually good?!</i>

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:54.570
What's wrong?! Answer already!

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:55.700
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:07.460
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.630
<i>If I don't answer soon...</i>

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:12.720
<i>That's it!</i>

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:17.720
What about a game based 
on rock-paper-scissors?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.470
Interesting.

00:15:19.470 --> 00:15:21.910
Looks like we've already got one good idea.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:28.610
I-I like... the rock-paper-scissors idea.

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.530
Rock-paper-scissors, eh?

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:38.160
Rejected! No rock-paper-scissors!

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:42.470
B-But you said it was a good idea before!

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:43.560
Shut up!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.920
Th-Then...

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.420
What about the human body puzzle?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.990
That idea is not happening!

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.060
Out of the question! Untouchable!

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.530
Th-Then...

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.940
Full-scale board game!

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:17.580
<i>Wh-What is that expression 
supposed to mean?!</i>

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:18.980
<i>It was an expression</i>

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:22.690
<i>that even Tonegawa, who had been President 
Hyoudou's right-hand-man for years,</i>

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:24.760
<i>had never seen before!</i>

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.200
<i>What now, Tonegawa?!</i>

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:28.440
<i>Which is it?!</i>

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.840
<b>Good</b>

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.840
<i>Is it good?! Is it bad?!</i>

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.840
<b>Bad</b>

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.730
<i>It's likely the latter...</i>

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.550
<i>That's definitely not a positive expression!</i>

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:38.350
That one's rejected, too! Rejected!

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.680
Rejected!

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:39.680
<b>Rejected!</b>

00:16:43.510 --> 00:16:46.310
Wh-What's that look for?!

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:48.310
Then which is it?!

00:16:48.310 --> 00:16:49.940
What?!

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:54.470
If you think none of those are good, 
which one do you like, Tonegawa-sensei?!

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.320
W-Well...

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:07.330
<b>Kawa</b>

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:07.330
<b>Yama</b>

00:16:58.650 --> 00:17:01.640
<i>D-Damn you, Kawasaki...</i>

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:05.160
<i>Wait, Yamazaki? I forget which one this is!</i>

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:07.330
<i>The bastard!</i>

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:19.160
<i>H-He passed the time bomb to me!</i>

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:25.390
<i>Biting the hand that feeds you?!</i>

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.640
<b>Bite!</b>

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:31.150
<i>You're just a man in black! 
Why has this happened to me?!</i>

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:34.150
An RPS-based game   Killer cops and robbers
Blood-draining Mahjong       Games of endurance
Clapping Game (Killer ver.)            Infinite Old Maid
Wild Animal battles   Full-Scale Board Game
Electrified jump rope                 Human Shogi
Dark poker               Monopoly man
UNO       Sky-high Rope Climb
Tag        Human Body Puzzle
Real Werewolf

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:34.150
<i>Wh-Which is it?</i>

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:37.410
<i>Which is the right answer?!</i>

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.530
<i>I don't know!</i>

00:17:41.480 --> 00:17:43.290
<i>I have no idea!</i>

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.800
<i>He only has one chance. 
There won't be another!</i>

00:17:46.800 --> 00:17:49.350
<i>Screwing up here will mean the end!</i>

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:52.130
<i>The career he's led until now, 
the trust, the support,</i>

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.300
<i>all of it will end!</i>

00:18:11.140 --> 00:18:12.690
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.070
Can you hear me, Tonegawa-se—

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.570
Shut up!

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:28.080
Quit yapping, dog.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:32.650
You don't need to ask again!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:36.780
This is my answer!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.140
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.770
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:51.650
Silence!

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:56.030
Not a single one of these 
ideas is good enough!

00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:59.990
The correct answer is to erase them all!

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.990
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.490
<i>That's right! The only way to 
avoid making a wrong decision...</i>

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.030
<i>The only obvious correct answer...</i>

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:11.500
<b>Choosing not to choose...!!</b>

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.500
<i>is to not choose at all!</i>

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.220
No way!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:21.280
But you were so—

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.710
It's not that simple!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:28.020
This project is too important to just 
proceed on without serious consideration!

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:33.520
There has to be something more! 
An outstanding idea!

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.390
<i>That's right!</i>

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:38.990
<i>Not only does he avoid taking any risk, 
he makes an appeal for more ideas!</i>

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:44.490
<i>A masterstroke to turn a 
crisis into an opportunity!</i>

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.060
Ultra C!

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.950
<b>Ultra C!</b>

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.000
Don't you agree, President?

00:19:56.530 --> 00:20:00.170
See?! He's nodding in agreement...

00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:23.910
<i>The truth is, it was after 10 PM.</i>

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:28.410
<i>A time when the elderly 
would generally be in bed.</i>

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:33.130
<i>Yes, and the king of Teiai, 
Hyoudou Kazutaka...</i>

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.750
<i>is still an old man!</i>

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:36.060
<b>Old Man!</b>

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.370
<i>In the end, he's still an old man!</i>

00:20:36.060 --> 00:20:38.190
<b>Old Man!!</b>

00:20:37.370 --> 00:20:40.130
I can't eat another bite...

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:47.450
<i>This whole time, he was trying... 
to not fall asleep?!</i>

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:50.180
<b>Meeting Room 3</b>

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:53.940
<i>Tonegawa is, once again, 
starting over from scratch!</i>

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.440
<i>But hang in there, Tonegawa!</i>

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:59.440
<i>Don't give up, Tonegawa!</i>

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:05.760
<i>This is the story of a lone man who struggles 
between his employer, the president,</i>

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:10.290
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:15.890
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:56.790
<i>Next time: Surefire.</i>

00:22:55.450 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Surefire</b>
